            "text_AW33tD": {
              "type": "text",
              "settings": {
                "text": "<p>Light Provisions began in an old Victorian house in Colorado Springs, and ten years later, I still make candles at home. I don’t really see that as something the business was supposed to outgrow. Making products in the same kind of space they’re ultimately meant to live in keeps me close to what matters: how they burn, how they smell, how they look on a table, and whether they actually make a room feel better.</p><p>I kept reaching for scents that were woodier, smokier, and more grounded than what I was finding elsewhere, so I started blending my own. Over time, those experiments developed into a house style built around balance and layering, with woods, resins, herbs, citrus, smoke, and other materials combined more like a well-made cocktail than a single-note fragrance.</p>",
                "width": "100%",
                "max_width": "narrow",
                "alignment": "left",
                "type_preset": "rte",
                "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                "font_size": "1rem",
